  "query_preview": "..Look for a mainly dry weather pattern well into next\nweek. A weak and dry flow develops aloft today, leading to light \nand variable surface winds at 5-10 mph under mainly clear skies \nwith nearly steady high/low temperatures.\n\nA weak trough drops southward across Arizona on Friday before \nheading further south over the weekend. As the trough passes \nthrough on Friday, there will be just enough lingering moisture \nand forcing for the development of instability showers over a few\nhigher terrain areas with daytime heating. Consequently, a slight\nchance of showers is expected over the Mogollon Rim, White \nMountains and Chuska Mountains Friday afternoon into the early \nevening. Any precipitation amounts will be minimal and snow levels\naround 9000' are forecast. Behind the trough on Saturday and \nSunday, high pressure will build over the Great Basin. Pressure \ngradients for north to northeast flow will then develop with \nlocally gusty winds developing, particularly Saturday. Most areas\nwill see north to northeast winds at 10-20 mph but for locations \nwhere northeast winds get funneled along and south to the Mogollon\nRim, with localized gusts of 30-40 mph likely based on latest \nensemble guidance.\n\nFor next week, it looks like fair weather will hold through at \nleast Wednesday with a lack of dynamics and dry northerly flow in\nplace.",
